DOWNLOAD SEQUENCING DATA FROM NCBI
We will use the NCBI Sequence Read Archive (SRA) to retrieve whole-genome sequencing (WGS) data from five Labrador Retrievers and five French Bulldogs.

Labrador Retriever Samples
prefetch SRR23628612
prefetch SRR29398833
prefetch SRR35557651
prefetch SRR23628673
prefetch SRR23628682

French Bulldog Samples
prefetch SRR23628665
prefetch SRR27051485
prefetch SRR23628636
prefetch SRR35533785
prefetch SRR35538214

After downloading the SRA files, convert them into FASTQ format using fasterq-dump.

bash
fasterq-dump SRR23628612 --split-files
Repeat for all 10 samples.

The --split-files option separates paired-end reads into forward and reverse FASTQ files when applicable.
FASTQ files will be used as input for downstream quality control and Bowtie2 alignment.
